## 1. Dashboard - Home Page

Learner PoV:
* As a learner, you will see Total Tasks, Completed, Outstanding, Progress% as soon as you log in so that you know your workload.

- Numbers calculated live from `tasks/{taskId}` where `userId == auth.uid`
- Formula: `total = tasks.length`, `completed = filter(completed).length`, `outstanding = total - completed`, `progress% = (completed/total)*100`
- Implemented in `dashboard.js` with `GET /tasks.json?auth=TOKEN` + `filter()` and `reduce()`

Assessor PoV ADDED:
* As an assessor, you want to view learner progress summary so you can monitor and identify who is falling behind.

- Assessor can `GET /tasks.json` and `GET /users.json` and calculate same metrics per learner
- Assessor view: filter `completed=false` to see outstanding work count per learner
- This solves the problem statement: "difficult for assessors to identify outstanding work"

## 2. Manage My Tasks - CRUD

Learner PoV:
* As a learner, you want 4 basic operations Create, Read, Update, Delete on your tasks like a to-do list but saved in Firebase.

C = Create
- Learner: Click "Add Task" fill Title "Complete Array Exercise", Due Date 15 Aug, Priority High, Category JavaScript. Validate `title.length>=3` and `dueDate >= today` before `POST /tasks/{taskId}.json`
- Assessor PoV ADDED: As assessor you want new tasks to have `userId` and `createdAt` so you can trace when learner created it and provide support if many high priority tasks created same day.

R = Read - View / Search / Filter / Sort
- Learner: Dashboard pulls `tasks` where `userId == currentUid` and displays via DOM `createElement`. Search title with `filter(t => t.title.includes(search))`, filter status `filter(t => t.completed==false)`, sort `sort((a,b)=> new Date(a.dueDate)-new Date(b.dueDate))` for "high priority due this week"
- Assessor PoV ADDED: As assessor you want to GET tasks/{taskId} filtered by userId and by category/priority so you can see relevant learner activity. E.g `GET /tasks.json` then `filter(userId==learnerId && priority==High)` to identify learners stuck on JavaScript.

U = Update
- Learner: Click task to edit title, dueDate, priority, category. Uses `PATCH /tasks/{taskId}.json?auth=TOKEN` for selected fields, `PUT` for full replace. Progress% recalculates automatically after update via `calculateProgress()`
- Assessor PoV ADDED: As assessor you want learner updates to be tracked with timestamp so you can see if learner updated task from outstanding to completed after support booking.

D = Delete
- Learner: Remove task from `tasks/{taskId}` in Firebase via `DELETE /tasks/{taskId}.json?auth`. Confirmation dialog `confirm("Delete this task? Cannot be undone")` before delete. Progress% recalculates after deletion.
- Assessor PoV ADDED: As assessor you want deletion to be owner-only `auth.uid == userId` so learners cannot delete other learners' tasks - enforced by security rules.

## 3. Book Support

Learner PoV:
* As a learner stuck on a function, you want to go to Book Support and fill topic, notes, preferredDate so you can get help.

- Saves to `bookings/{bookingId}` with `status: pending`, `userId: auth.uid`
- Validation: topic required, preferredDate not past
- `POST /bookings/{bookingId}.json?auth`

Assessor PoV ADDED:
* As an assessor, you want to view all bookings with status pending and PATCH status to Confirmed/Rejected so learner gets feedback.

- Assessor flow: `GET /bookings.json?auth` -> `FILTER status==pending` -> `PATCH /bookings/{id}.json {"status":"approved"}`
- Security: `".write": "auth != null"` for creation, admin check `root.child('users/'+auth.uid+'/role').val()=='admin'` for status update
- Learner then sees updated status feedback on dashboard.

## 4. Play Mini Game - Resources Page

Learner PoV:
* As a learner, when you open Resources you want to play a mini-game to relax and track coding skills.

- Built with http://Phaser.js / http://Kaboom.js, game loop with `setInterval`
- Score saved via `POST /scores/{scoreId}.json` with `userId, score, duration, completedAt`

Assessor PoV ADDED:
* As an assessor, you want to see scores/{scoreId} per learner to gauge engagement and problem-solving persistence.

- `GET /scores.json` filtered by `userId` to see attempts and duration
- Not for grading, for support motivation.

## 5. Your Preferences Stick - Cookies

Learner PoV:
* As a learner you want to switch to Dark Mode and have it remembered next login.

- Saved as `document.cookie = "theme=dark; max-age=3600; path=/; SameSite=Lax"`
- NO password, NO personal data in cookie - only non-sensitive prefs
- On load: `document.cookie.split()` to read theme

Assessor PoV ADDED:
* As an assessor, you want preferences to be non-sensitive only so system complies with safety policy and no learner data leaks via cookies.

## 6. Print Summary

Learner PoV:
* As a learner at end of week you want to click Print Progress Summary to create PDF of progress, tasks completed, and bookings.

- Uses `calculateProgress()` + `reduce()` for totalHours
- `window.print()` creates printable view, `progress.html` with `@media print`
- Includes list from `filter(completed==true)` and `bookings`

Assessor PoV ADDED:
* As an assessor, you want printable summaries per learner for offline reviews and intervention meetings.

- Assessor can print learner-specific report: `GET /tasks` + `GET /bookings` filtered by `userId`

## 7. Data Safety - REST + Rules

Both PoV:
* As a user you want all actions to use Firebase REST API GET, POST, PATCH, PUT, DELETE with auth token.

- Learner can only `read/write where userId == auth.uid`
- No public write: Root rule `".write": false`
- Validation before fetch, try/catch with feedback
- http://service-account.json in `.gitignore`

## 8. Log Out

Learner PoV:
* As a learner you want to log out securely so no one accesses my data.

- Confirmation dialog `confirm("Are you sure you want to sign out?")`
- Calls `signOut(auth)`, clears auth state, `window.location.href="index.html"`

Assessor PoV ADDED:
* As an assessor, you want sign out to clear auth token so shared devices don't expose learner data.

